  "decision": "Approved",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the end of three years from the date of this permission. \r\rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\rE00, E01, E02, E03, E04, E05, P01, P02, P03, P04, P05 and P06, SuDS proforma, Highway Safety Impact Assessment & CIL form\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied until the 6 long stay cycle parking spaces have been fully constructed in accordance with the hereby approved details and shall thereafter be retained for the lifetime of the development.  \r \rReason: To ensure that adequate cycle parking facilities are provided to promote sustainable modes of transport. \r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied until waste storage and recycling facilities to satisfy the future number of occupiers on site have been provided within the development, in accordance with the Enfield's Household Recycling and Waste Planning Guidance for New Developments (February 2024). Such facilities to be retained permanently thereafter.\r\rReason: To ensure that adequate waste and recycling storage facilities are provided to meet the needs of future occupiers, promote sustainable waste management practices, and support borough-wide recycling targets. \r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied by more than six residents at any one time without first obtaining the approval, in writing, of the Local Planning Authority.  \r \rReason: To ensure that the future occupation of the building does not adversely affect the adjoining premises/immediate \r",
    "No cooking facilities, including hot plates, shall be installed in the bedrooms of the development hereby permitted unless details have first been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. Any cooking facilities shall thereafter only be implemented in accordance with the details that have been approved pursuant to this condition. \r \rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area. \r\r"
  ],
